            <ArticleTitle>Acute Glucose Response Properties Beyond Feeding.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>356-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.molmed.2016.03.001</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1471-4914(16)00053-8</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Hypothalamic AgRP neurons potently coordinate feeding behavior to ensure an organism's viability. However, their acute role in glucose-regulatory function remains to be addressed. Steculorum et al. now report that activation of a specific set of AgRP neurons results in an impairment of insulin-stimulated glucose uptake in brown fat through a myogenic signature program.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Published by Elsevier Ltd.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
